.Dd April 29, 2026
.Dt PKG-RWHICH 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm "pkg rwhich"
.Nd display which remote package provides a specific file
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl gq
.Op Fl r Ar reponame
.Ar file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
queries the repository catalogues to find which remote package provides the
specified
.Ar file .
.Pp
This requires that the repository was created with the
.Fl l
flag to
.Xr pkg-repo 8
.Pq to generate the file listing ,
and that the client has run
.Xr pkg-update 8
to fetch the file metadata.
.Pp
Unlike
.Xr pkg-which 8 ,
which searches locally installed packages,
.Nm
searches the remote repository catalogues.
.Pp
In glob mode (
.Fl g
) ,
the pattern is split into a directory part and a filename part at the
last slash.
If the directory part contains no glob metacharacters, only files in
the matching directory are tested, which significantly speeds up the search.
Patterns without any slash are matched against the filename only,
regardless of the directory.
.Sh OPTIONS
The following options are supported by
.Nm :
.Bl -tag -width repository
.It Fl g , Cm --glob
Treat
.Ar file
as a glob pattern.
.It Fl q , Cm --quiet
Be quiet.
Only print the package name and version, one per line.
.It Fl r Ar reponame , Cm --repository Ar reponame
Limit the search to the named repository.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Find which package provides a specific binary:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ pkg rwhich /usr/local/bin/bash
/usr/local/bin/bash is provided by package bash-5.2.26_2
.Ed
.Pp
Find all packages providing a shared library with a filename-only pattern:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ pkg rwhich -g 'libcurl*'
/usr/local/lib/libcurl.so is provided by package curl-8.7.1
/usr/local/lib/libcurl.so.4 is provided by package curl-8.7.1
.Ed
.Pp
Find packages in a specific directory (fast path, directory is matched exactly):
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ pkg rwhich -g '/usr/local/bin/python*'
/usr/local/bin/python3.11 is provided by package python311-3.11.9
/usr/local/bin/python3 is provided by package python3-3.11.9
.Ed
.Pp
Find files across all directories with a wildcard directory pattern:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ pkg rwhich -g '*/bin/ls'
/usr/bin/ls is provided by package FreeBSD-runtime-15.1p1
/usr/local/bin/ls is provided by package coreutils-9.5
.Ed
.Pp
In glob mode, the real file path is displayed for each match, not the glob pattern.
.Pp
Quiet mode for scripting:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ pkg rwhich -q /usr/local/bin/python3.11
python311-3.11.9
.Ed
.Pp
Multiple files can be queried in a single invocation:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ pkg rwhich /usr/local/bin/bash /usr/local/bin/zsh
/usr/local/bin/bash is provided by package bash-5.2.26_2
/usr/local/bin/zsh is provided by package zsh-5.9
.Ed
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
The following environment variables affect the execution of
.Nm .
See
.Xr pkg.conf 5
for further description.
.Bl -tag -width ".Ev NO_DESCRIPTIONS"
.It Ev PKG_DBDIR
.It Ev PKG_RWHICH_DATABASE
.It Ev REPOS_DIR
.El
.Sh CONFIGURATION
.Nm
is controlled by two configuration options described in
.Xr pkg.conf 5 :
.Bl -tag -width ".Cm PKG_RWHICH_DATABASE"
.It Cm PKG_RWHICH_DATABASE
Global boolean option (default:
.Cm YES ).
When set to
.Cm NO ,
disables rwhich for all repositories regardless of per-repository settings.
.It Cm RWHICH_DATABASE
Per-repository boolean option (default:
.Cm YES ).
When set to
.Cm NO ,
the file listing database is not downloaded for that specific repository
and
.Nm
will not search it.
.El
